questions.answer:
10 20
{'_field_x': 10, '_field_y': 20}

__set_name__ is called by the metaclass during class creation, providing the attribute name. Each Field instance stores a unique private key (_field_x, _field_y) so multiple descriptors coexist without colliding in the instance __dict__.

